  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Best Western Plus Hôtel Brice Garden is a 4-star hotel in central Nice, rue Maréchal Joffre, about 200 metres from the Promenade des Anglais according to the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office. Its picture windows open onto terraces and a private garden planted with Mediterranean species, with a fountain; breakfast is taken in a bright room overlooking this garden. The hotel holds the Green Key label and the Pet Friendly Nice Côte d'Azur label.</p>

      <h2>The hotel</h2>
      <p>The establishment has 59 rooms in a Mediterranean, modern style, air-conditioned, with minibar, safe and free wifi; some have a large balcony, and three are adapted for guests with reduced mobility. It is open all year, with a 24-hour reception. The sweet-and-savoury breakfast buffet is served from 7am to 11am (€20 per person according to the hotel's website), with an express takeaway option early in the morning or late in the morning. Parking is a set of covered garages 150 metres away, on request and subject to availability, limited to 1.85 m in height. Guests also have access to a private beach at a preferential rate, and a luggage room with a courtesy shower lets you enjoy the city before arrival or after departure.</p>

      <h2>With a dog</h2>
      <p>The "Services" page and the FAQ of the hotel's website state that small animals under 10 kg are welcomed free of charge, with a bowl and a few treats, and that they are admitted throughout the establishment except the breakfast room. For an animal over 10 kg, the hotel asks to be contacted before booking. Its presence must be announced when booking. The hotel's page on bestwestern.com, for its part, states a charge of €15 per night and asks you to specify the species, breed and size of the animal; the tourist office mentions "Animals with supplement".</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: breakfast is off-limits to me, but the hotel itself suggests bringing a little treat up to the room. I approve.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Promenade des Anglais, Place Masséna, the Old Town and the pedestrian shopping streets are all within walking distance; Nice-Ville station is close. Before taking your dog to a Nice beach, check the municipal rules in force.</p>
